After having ascended once in vanilla Nethack with an Elven wizard, and being 
able to do fairly well with Elven wizards, I tried Slash'EM for a change, and 
found it to be *really* hard; you're not even guraunteed a Force Bolt 
spellbook.  To make things not quite as hard, I hacked the source so that, of 
the four starting spellbooks, a wizard will always have a Force Bolt and 
Magic Missile spell books, Elven wizards will always have a Resist Poison 
spellbook (instead of 50% chance of Resist Sleep, which is useless to an 
Elf), plus always start with a blindfold and a magic marker, where there is 
usually a 1/5 chance of each of them being in the initial inventory.

I'm wondering if people would like a more general version of this, that could 
be done with a setting.  Either on the command line or in the options file, 
you'd specify an easiness level, 1 or up (or negative to make it more 
difficult), which would alter your initial inventory to make things easier, 
and maybe also change the generation of random inventory items, so that, say, 
you'll never get a potion of water or fruit juice, or a mood ring.

So, how does that sound?


